# Privacy Policy — Talking Mouse

**Last updated:** June 6, 2026

Talking Mouse is a Chrome browser extension that recommends YouTube videos based on the user's inferred affective state. Affective state is inferred from mouse trajectory patterns using an on-device machine learning classifier.

This privacy policy describes what data the extension accesses, what it does NOT access, and how that data is handled.

---

## What the extension collects

The extension's content script captures the following from each web page the user visits:

- Cursor x/y coordinates (in CSS pixels)
- Mouse event type (`mousemove`, `mousedown`, `mouseup`)
- Mouse button identifier (for click events only)
- Local millisecond timestamp

All captured events are held only in a rolling 60-second buffer inside the extension's local service worker.

## What the extension does NOT collect

- Page content, DOM structure, or rendered text
- Page URLs, page titles, or browsing history
- Text typed into forms, search boxes, or input fields
- Login credentials, passwords, payment data, or any other identifying information
- Audio, video, microphone, camera, or any other sensor data
- Clipboard contents
- Personally identifiable information of any kind

## Where data is processed

All captured mouse data is processed entirely on the user's device. The Random Forest classifier that infers affective state runs locally inside the extension's service worker.

**No mouse data is ever transmitted to any server**, including the developer's own infrastructure.

## Outbound network requests

The extension makes network requests only to the following endpoint:

- `https://www.googleapis.com/youtube/v3/*` — YouTube Data API v3, to fetch video recommendations matching the user's inferred state. Only the search query string (for example, `"lofi study music"`) and the YouTube API key are sent. No mouse data is included.

YouTube's privacy policy: https://policies.google.com/privacy

## Local storage

The extension uses `chrome.storage.local` (device-local, never synced to any Google account) to persist:

- The user's YouTube Data API v3 key
- The user's affect-regulation strategy preference per arousal state
- The user's content type filter preference (any video vs. music-only)

No browsing data, no captured mouse data, and no analytics are written to storage.

## How to delete stored data

To delete all data stored by the extension:

1. Visit `chrome://extensions` in Chrome
2. Find "Talking Mouse"
3. Click "Remove" (uninstalls the extension and clears all its storage)

Alternatively, in the extension's popup, open the developer console and run:
`chrome.storage.local.clear()`

## Third-party services

The only third-party service the extension contacts is YouTube Data API v3, owned and operated by Google LLC. Use of the YouTube API is subject to Google's terms and privacy policy:

- YouTube API Terms of Service: https://developers.google.com/youtube/terms/api-services-terms-of-service
- Google Privacy Policy: https://policies.google.com/privacy

## Children's privacy

Talking Mouse is not directed at children under 13 years of age. The developer does not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has used this extension, contact the developer at the email below and any stored preferences will be removed.

## Research context

This extension is built on academic research conducted by the developer. The classifier was trained on a controlled-task dataset collected under informed consent from adult participants. No data from extension users is collected, retained, or used for research purposes.

